{
  "title": "Things Taught by the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) to Lady Fatimah (s.a.)",
  "data": "Before going to sleep, recite [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) 3 times.\nInvoke Almighty Allah's blessings upon the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and the prophets who came before him.\nImplore Almighty Allah's forgiveness for the believers.\nSay these four doxological statements:\nسُبْحَانَ اللهِ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ‏ وَلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَاللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ.\nSUBHAANAL LAAHE WAL HAMDO LILLAAHE WA LAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO WAL LAAHO AKBARO.\nGlory be to Allah, and all praise is due to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest.",
  "merits": "In the book of Khulasat al-Azkaar, Lady Fatimah al-Zahra’ (s.a.) is reported to have said: I had just spread out my bed when my father the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) visited me. “Fatimah,” he said. “Do not go to sleep before You do four things: recite the Holy Qur’an entirely, make all prophets to intercede for you, win the pleasure of all believers with you, and win the reward of one hajj and one umrah.” I answered, “Allah’s Messenger, you have just ordered me to do four things none of which I can do while I am in this situation of mine!” With smile, the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said, “If you recite [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) three times, you will be decided as having recited the Holy Qur’an entirely. If you invoke Almighty Allah’s blessings upon me and the prophets who came before me, we all will intercede for you on the Resurrection Day. If you implore Almighty Allah’s forgiveness for the believers, they all will be pleased with you. If you repeat these four doxological statements, you will be decided as having performed hajj and ‘umrah.”"
}
